        }
      },
      "results": [
        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-89: Improper Neutralization of Special Elements used in an SQL Command ('SQL Injection')",
          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": "SQL Injection in /api/user/search via username Parameter: - **Source**: Untrusted user input enters the endpoint via `request.args.get('username', '')` on line 65.\n- **Sanitization/Validation**: No validation, escaping, or parameterization is performed. The string is directly interpolated into the SQL query using an f-string.\n- **Sink**: The constructed query string is passed directly into `cursor.execute(query)` on line 72.\n- **Data Flow**: The attacker provides a crafted `username` query parameter -> Flask parses it into `username` -> f-string formatting injects raw SQL into `query` -> `cursor.execute(query)` executes the statement against the SQLite database.\n\n**Conceptual Exploit Payload**:\nSend a GET request with an SQL injection payload in the `username` parameter to extract all user records or bypass authentication:\n```http\nGET /api/user/search?username=%27+OR+1%3D1+-- HTTP/1.1\nHost: localhost:5000\n```\nWhen formatted, the query becomes:\n`SELECT id, username, email, role FROM users WHERE username = '' OR 1=1 --'`\nThis forces the WHERE clause to evaluate to true for every record in the `users` table, returning all users."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "app.py"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 70,
                  "endLine": 72
                }
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-78: Improper Neutralization of Special Elements used in an OS Command ('OS Command Injection')",
          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": "OS Command Injection in /api/tools/ping via host Parameter: - **Source**: Untrusted user input enters the endpoint via the JSON request payload field `host` (`data.get('host', '')`) on line 107.\n- **Sanitization/Validation**: The application only checks that the field is non-empty (`if not host:`). It performs no validation, whitelisting (e.g. IP address or hostname validation), or shell escaping.\n- **Sink**: The unvalidated string is formatted into `command = f\"ping -c 1 {host}\"` and executed directly via `os.system(command)` on line 114, which spawns a system shell (`/bin/sh -c`).\n- **Data Flow**: The client posts a JSON payload containing shell metacharacters -> `host` is extracted -> String interpolation constructs the shell command -> `os.system` executes the command with shell interpretation, executing attacker-supplied commands with the privileges of the web application process.\n\n**Conceptual Exploit Payload**:\nSend a POST request with command chaining operators (e.g., `;`, `&&`, or `|`) in the `host` parameter:\n```http\nPOST /api/tools/ping HTTP/1.1\nHost: localhost:5000\nContent-Type: application/json\n\n{\n  \"host\": \"127.0.0.1; cat /etc/passwd\"\n}\n```\nThe resulting shell execution will run `ping -c 1 127.0.0.1` followed by `cat /etc/passwd`."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "app.py"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 113,
                  "endLine": 114
                }
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-89",
          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": "SQL Injection in /api/user/search via username Parameter: - **Source**: Untrusted user input enters the endpoint via `request.args.get('username', '')` on line 65.\n- **Sanitization/Validation**: No validation, escaping, or parameterization is performed. The string is directly interpolated into the SQL query using an f-string.\n- **Sink**: The constructed query string is passed directly into `cursor.execute(query)` on line 72.\n- **Data Flow**: The attacker provides a crafted `username` query parameter -> Flask parses it into `username` -> f-string formatting injects raw SQL into `query` -> `cursor.execute(query)` executes the statement against the SQLite database.\n\n**Conceptual Exploit Payload**:\nSend a GET request with an SQL injection payload in the `username` parameter to extract all user records or bypass authentication:\n```http\nGET /api/user/search?username=%27+OR+1%3D1+-- HTTP/1.1\nHost: localhost:5000\n```\nWhen formatted, the query becomes:\n`SELECT id, username, email, role FROM users WHERE username = '' OR 1=1 --'`\nThis forces the WHERE clause to evaluate to true for every record in the `users` table, returning all users."
